KPL/MYB

UTC: TAI - UTC since 1960
=========================

   TAI - UTC = OFFSET + (MJD - DRIFT_MJD) * DRIFT_RATE                   [seconds]

   MJD is the UTC Modified Julian Date including the fraction of the day. A row is
   in force from 0h UTC of its START_MJD until the start of the next row; the last
   row stays in force until VALID_UNTIL_MJD (exclusive), the expiry announced by the
   IERS. After that date conversions fail with MYB_E_RANGE instead of guessing
   whether a leap second was inserted. Before 1972 UTC seconds were not SI seconds
   (the rate terms) and the steps were fractional.

Update procedure: when IERS Bulletin C announces a leap second, append a row with
the new START_MJD and OFFSET (DRIFT_MJD = DRIFT_RATE = 0) and move VALID_UNTIL_MJD to
the new expiry date of https://hpiers.obspm.fr/iers/bul/bulc/Leap_Second.dat.

Sources
   1960-1971: USNO tai-utc.dat as tabulated in ERFA src/dat.c (BSD-3-Clause,
              derived from SOFA iau_DAT), revision 1a8044cde5b7763295d472a6443387239127c6c8.
   1972-:     IERS Leap_Second.dat, "Updated through IERS Bulletin 72 issued in
              July 2026", "File expires on 28 June 2027"; every row checked against
              the ERFA table.

Columns below: START_MJD, OFFSET (s), DRIFT_MJD, DRIFT_RATE (s/day), date (comment).

